{"data":[{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.11155","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.11155","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2509.11155","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Santhosh G","familyName":"S","name":"S, Santhosh G","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Saurav","familyName":"Prakash","name":"Prakash, Saurav","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Balaraman","familyName":"Ravindran","name":"Ravindran, Balaraman","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"AQUA: Attention via QUery mAgnitudes for Memory and Compute Efficient Inference in LLMs"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2025,"subjects":[{"subject":"Machine Learning (cs.LG)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Computation and Language (cs.CL)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2025-09-14T08:20:48Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-09-16T00:38:02Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-09","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[{"rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"The quadratic complexity of the attention mechanism remains a fundamental barrier to scaling Large Language Models (LLMs) to longer contexts, creating a critical bottleneck in both computation and memory. To address this, we introduce AQUA (Attention via QUery mAgnitudes) a novel and versatile approximation strategy that significantly reduces the cost of attention with a graceful performance trade-off. Our method operates in two phases: an efficient offline step where we compute a universal, language agnostic projection matrix via SVD on a calibration dataset, and an online inference step where we project query and key vectors and dynamically select a sparse subset of dimensions based on the query's magnitude. We provide a formal theoretical analysis of AQUA, establishing the break-even point at which it becomes more computationally efficient than standard attention. Our empirical evaluations on state-of-the-art models like Llama-3.1-8B demonstrate that a 25% reduction in the attention dot-product computation can be achieved with a statistically insignificant impact on performance across a wide range of benchmarks. We further showcase the versatility of AQUA by demonstrating its ability to synergistically accelerate existing token eviction methods like H2O and to directly reduce KV-cache memory size. By offering a controllable knob to balance efficiency and accuracy, AQUA provides a practical and powerful tool for making large-scale LLM inference more accessible and sustainable."}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.11155","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2025-09-16T02:56:02Z","registered":"2025-09-16T02:56:03Z","published":null,"updated":"2025-09-16T02:56:03Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}}],"meta":{"total":1,"totalPages":1,"page":1},"links":{"self":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?client-id=arxiv.content\u0026query=subjects.subject%3A%28%22cs.CL%22+OR+%22cs.LG%22%29+AND+%28titles.title%3A%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+transformer+OR+transformers+OR+%22mixture+of+experts%22+OR+%22mixture-of-experts%22+OR+%22foundation+model%22+OR+%22foundation+models%22%29+OR+descriptions.description%3A%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+transformer+OR+transformers+OR+%22mixture+of+experts%22+OR+%22mixture-of-experts%22+OR+%22foundation+model%22+OR+%22foundation+models%22%29%29+AND+%28titles.title%3A%28architecture+OR+architectures+OR+attention+OR+optimization+OR+optimisation+OR+training+OR+%22post-training%22+OR+posttraining%29+OR+descriptions.description%3A%28architecture+OR+architectures+OR+attention+OR+optimization+OR+optimisation+OR+training+OR+%22post-training%22+OR+posttraining%29%29+AND+doi%3A%2210.48550%2Farxiv.2509.11155%22+AND+registered%3A%5B2025-09-16T00%3A00%3A00Z+TO+2025-09-16T23%3A59%3A59Z%5D\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=10"}}